=== WHAT THIS PROVES (the Wave-8 quantization milestone) ===
An int8 WEIGHT-ONLY quantized matmul (kernels/generated/matmul_int8.cu) compiles clean
for nvcc sm_80 AND sm_90 (GPU-free PTX) AND compiles + RUNS on the RX 7800 XT (gfx1101,
hipcc), and passes the QUANTIZATION-AWARE golden (tests/golden/quant_golden.py — a NEW
golden module; the shared golden.py/metrics.py are UNCHANGED) under the RELAXED quant
thresholds (cosine >= 0.99, max_rel_err <= 5e-2, pcc >= 0.99). The fp8 (e4m3fn/e5m2)
path is a SIMULATION (NO fp8 hardware): weights are rounded onto the fp8 grid (ml_dtypes
float8 in the golden; a portable RNE round in the CPU ref) and matmul'd in bf16/fp32 —
the CPU ref matches the golden BIT-EXACTLY for uniform [-1,1] weights.

int8 weight-only is a codegen VARIANT of the CLOSED `polykernel.matmul` op (NO new op, NO
new declared attribute); `path=int8_weight_only` is a report annotation (contract H),
exactly as `path=wmma` is for the WMMA variant. The tiled bf16 SCALAR baseline
(kernels/generated/matmul.cu) is UNCHANGED and remains the correctness reference.

=== QUANTIZATION CONTRACT (matches tests/golden/quant_golden.py) ===
int8 weight-only, per output channel (per column of W[K,N]), symmetric:
    amax[n] = max_k |W[k,n]|;  scale[n] = amax[n]/127   (fp32; all-zero channel -> scale=1)
    wq[k,n] = clip(round(W[k,n]/scale[n]), -127, 127)    (int8, round-to-nearest-even)
    dequant: w_deq[k,n] = wq[k,n] * scale[n]             (fp32, per output channel n)
    C[m,n]  = bf16( sum_k fp32(A[m,k]) * (fp32(Wq[k,n]) * scale[n]) )   (fp32 accum, bf16 RNE out)
Activations A stay bf16 — only the WEIGHTS are int8 (weight-only). The kernel dequantizes
on the fly inside the inner loop (acc += bf16(As) * (float(Bs_int8) * scale[col])).
fp8 simulation (weights only): w_fp8 = W.astype(float8_e4m3fn|float8_e5m2).astype(fp32);
    C = bf16( fp32(bf16(A)) @ w_fp8 ).  NO fp8 hardware — a simulation (labelled as such).

